Interoperability attribution: the gaze-bus WebSocket message shape consumed by
dwell.js ({gazePoint:{x,y}, validity, timestamp} on a localhost port, plus a
GET /status endpoint) was adopted for interoperability from Aivota AAC's gaze
sidecar contract, with the developer's knowledge from a July 2026
collaboration. The implementation here is entirely independent. The post-fire
reactivation-anchor behavior in dwell.js was likewise inspired by Aivota (and
is credited in-source); the mechanism differs.

dwell.js's smoothing/selection model draws on published prior art including the
One-Euro filter (Casiez, Roussel, Vogel 2012) and dwell-selection patterns from
the open-source OptiKey project.
